a spinner. Same app, same minute. A ping cannot click a button, so it passes straight over failures like these. A signup form that returns 200 and silently drops the confirmation request. A Stripe card iframe that stops mounting after a CSP header change. A login that loops to /login?error=state after an Auth0 rule edit. Before What your uptime check saw GET https://app.acme.dev/ → 200 OK · 183 ms · SSL valid for 61 days. Status: Up. Everything green. Your status page agrees. After What a customer saw 8 steps. Step 7 click "Pay $29" → POST /api/checkout/confirm returned 502 after 8.2 s. "Payment confirmed" never appeared. Status: Failed. Nobody in eu-west or ap-south has paid you since 03:12 UTC. See a full failed run PLAYWRIGHT MONITORING The spec you run in CI  is the monitor you run in production Upload your Playwright project, name the entry spec, and pick a schedule. Same selectors, same assertions, same @playwright/test. Your own specs, unchanged. If it passes with npx playwright test, it is a candidate check. Upload through the package API. Include the files the spec imports. Secrets reach the spec as process.env.NAME. DevHelm finds the names in your files, stores the values encrypted, and masks them in network logs, HAR, console and runner logs. Screenshots and video show whatever the page shows, so run the check with a dedicated test account. 1 Upload your spec 2 Pick regions and schedule 3 First run, with its trace Read how to upload a spec tests/checkout.spec.ts What you upload import { test, expect } from '@playwright/test';

test('pro plan checkout completes', async ({ page }) => {
  await test.step('Open login', () => page.goto('https://app.acme.dev/login'));
  await test.step('Sign in', async () => {
    await page.getByLabel('Email').fill(process.env.CHECKOUT_EMAIL!);
    await page.getByLabel('Password').fill(process.env.CHECKOUT_PASSWORD!);
    await page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Sign in' }).click();
  });
  await test.step('Open pricing', () => page.goto('https://app.acme.dev/pricing'));
  await test.step('Start Pro', () => page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Start Pro' }).click());

  const card = page.frameLocator('iframe[name^="__privateStripeFrame"]').first();
  await test.step('Enter card', () => card.getByPlaceholder('Card number').fill('4242 4242 4242 4242'));
  await test.step('Enter expiry and CVC', async () => {
    await card.getByPlaceholder('MM / YY').fill('12 / 34');
    await card.getByPlaceholder('CVC').fill('123');
  });
  await test.step('Pay $29', () => page.getByRole('button', { name: /Pay \$29/ }).click());
  await test.step('Payment confirmed', () =>
    expect(page.getByRole('heading', { name: 'Payment confirmed' })).toBeVisible({ timeout: 15_000 })
  );
}); checkout-monitor.zip
